The profile shows `torch.bmm` is not the main limiter for large `N`; it is close to 1 ms for `1024`. Most of the time is in input LayerNorm, the five hidden projections, and final output projection/normalization. I’m going to test alternate routing between the fused FP16 path and the cuBLAS-heavy BF16 path by shape.
